    <briefdescription>
<para>Policy denial exception — thrown when an export is rejected by PolicyEngine. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is the concrete typed wrapper used by exporter paths that surface <computeroutput>ERR_EXPORT_POLICY_DENIED</computeroutput> via <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1exporters_1_1_exporter_exception" kindref="compound">ExporterException</ref></computeroutput>. Catching <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1exporters_1_1_exporter_exception" kindref="compound">ExporterException</ref></computeroutput> remains the stable contract for policy-blocked export operations.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>isResumableError(ExporterErrorCode::EXPORT_ABORTED) == false — policy denials are fail-closed and never resumable. The operator or requesting user must resolve the policy conflict before re-attempting. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
